## IP Addressing & Subnetting

### IPv4 Private Ranges (RFC 1918)
- **Class A** — `10.0.0.0/8` (large orgs)
- **Class B** — `172.16.0.0/12` (medium)
- **Class C** — `192.168.0.0/16` (home/SOHO)

### CIDR Notation
- `/24` = 256 IPs (254 usable)
- `/16` = 65,536 IPs
- `/32` = single host
- First & last IPs in a subnet are reserved (network + broadcast)

### Key Concepts
- **NAT** — Translates private IPs to a public IP at the router. Private IPs never route on the internet.
- **IPv6** — 128-bit addresses. `::1` = loopback. `fe80::` = link-local. Most networks run dual-stack (IPv4 + IPv6).

