## Key Protocols & Ports

| Port | Protocol | Notes |
|------|----------|-------|
| TCP 80 / 443 | HTTP / HTTPS | Web traffic. 443 = TLS encrypted |
| TCP/UDP 53 | DNS | Resolves names → IPs. Common attack vector |
| TCP 22 | SSH | Encrypted remote shell. Replaces Telnet |
| TCP 23 | Telnet | Cleartext shell — **never use**, fully sniffable |
| TCP 21 | FTP | Cleartext credentials — use SFTP instead |
| TCP 25 | SMTP | Email sending. Abused for spam & phishing |
| UDP 67/68 | DHCP | Auto-assigns IP, gateway, DNS to clients |
| ICMP | Ping / Traceroute | Network diagnostics. Used in recon |
| TCP 445 | SMB | Windows file sharing. EternalBlue target |
| TCP 3389 | RDP | Windows remote desktop. Brute-force target |

