## TCP 3-Way Handshake

```
Client          Server
  |--- SYN ------->|   "I want to connect"
  |<-- SYN-ACK ----|   "OK, acknowledged"
  |--- ACK ------->|   "Connected!"
```

### Security relevance
- **SYN flood attack** — Attacker sends thousands of SYNs but never sends the final ACK, exhausting the server's connection table (classic DoS).
- **Nmap SYN scan (`-sS`)** — Sends SYN, gets SYN-ACK (open) or RST (closed), never completes the handshake. Stealthier than a full connect scan.

