## Defense — Tools & Concepts

### Firewalls
| Type | Description |
|------|-------------|
| Packet filter | Blocks by IP/port rules (stateless) |
| Stateful | Tracks connection state |
| WAF | Inspects HTTP, blocks SQLi/XSS at layer 7 |
| NGFW | Deep packet inspection + application awareness |

### IDS vs IPS
- **IDS** — Detects & alerts (passive, out-of-band)
- **IPS** — Detects & blocks (inline, active)
- **Signature-based** — Matches known attack patterns
- **Anomaly-based** — Flags deviations from baseline behaviour
- Tools: Snort, Suricata, Zeek

### Network Segmentation
- **VLANs** — Logical network separation at layer 2
- **DMZ** — Isolates public-facing servers from internal network
- **Zero trust** — Verify every request regardless of source
- Limits blast radius of a breach

### Encryption in Transit
- **TLS 1.3** — Current standard for HTTPS
- **VPN** — IPSec or WireGuard tunnels for secure remote access
- **SSH** — Secure shell, file transfer (SCP/SFTP), and tunneling
- Always validate certificate chains; watch for self-signed certs in prod

